    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0955" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg934"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1115/11–2448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-24T13:00:00+03:00">November 24,
                            1948—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2723. Since return, I have reviewed question possible prisoner exchange and if
                    Berlin still regards initiation project difficult on lines suggested Embtel 496,
                    November 20 (repeated Department 2691<anchor n="1" xml:id="d627-f1"/>), I am
                    prepared to take up here at Gusev<anchor n="2" xml:id="d627-f2"/> level. While
                    approach through repatriation channels would obviate main possibilities Soviet
                    propaganda or complaints re non-included cases, I am persuaded only hope release
                    American citizens detained here lies in such trade. I should not like to see
                    such hope lost by failure on our part make every effort within reason.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2723, repeated USPolad Berlin 501.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d627-f1" n="1" xml:id="d627-f1-content">
